# Upstream-owned suites bin/fm-lint.sh's fixture-write purity check skips.
#
# Each line is one repository-relative path, matched exactly; `#` lines and
# blank lines are ignored. A file belongs here only when upstream owns it: it
# exists in upstream's tree and this fleet carries it in upstream's text,
# possibly plus fleet hunks. Listing it keeps upstream's plain-redirect spelling
# legal there, so a take-in returns the file as upstream wrote it instead of
# converting it to fm_fakebin_write.
#
# Listing a file takes ALL of it out of the scan, fleet hunks included, so the
# lint no longer backstops them: a fleet hunk added to a listed file must still
# write every fixture stub through fm_fakebin_write by hand, and only
# upstream's own lines may keep a plain redirect.
#
# Never list a fleet-owned suite, a fleet `-fleet` sibling, or a shared helper
# (tests/lib.sh, tests/fixtures.sh, and the other sourced *-helpers.sh files):
# fleet code keeps the carrier, and every path not named here stays checked.
# When a take-in brings a new upstream suite whose plain redirect fails the
# check, add its path here rather than converting it.
# tests/fakebin-write.sh owns the hazard this check guards against.

